--- v9 fix (agent/crustle_rules.py; the ONE validated lever) ---
MIST-BLANKS-POWERFUL-HAND: Powerful Hand (743) does its damage by PLACING counters — an attack
EFFECT — and Mist Energy prevents all attack effects on its holder ("Damage is not an effect").
v8 attached Mist LAST (tie 0.0 < Grow Grass 0.9). v9: vs a visible counter-effect line
{741,742,743,245} the first Mist on an un-Misted target gets tie 1.5 (still < the 30-pt rung
gaps) + promote an already-Misted wall (+60 in placement contexts).
Mechanism verified in-engine (probe): misted 150HP Crustle took 8 consecutive Powerful Hands
for ZERO damage; their draw engine then decked itself out (t11-22).
Their counterplay observed: Enhanced Hammer strips the Mist (we re-mist), Boss's Orders farms
un-misted bench.
NOT Munkidori 112: its counter-moving is an ABILITY (Mist blocks attack effects only); including
it cost -2.4pt vs Tea Party over n=800 -> removed.

Rejected after individual arms (kept out of the ship):
* Mist-any-Crustle rung boost (L1e): alakazam arm 15.5 -> 11.5 (worse; active 3-energy matters).
* Cheren deck-parity governor (2 variants): mirror 55.8 -> 51.5 / 48.8 trend-negative; its
  target (2 ladder deck-outs) is locally unmeasurable. Rejected.
* Poffin bench-stock vs counter family (L3b): +1.7 at n=400/arm — noise, not provable. Rejected.

